// Where the units start.
//
// This is a scaffold for trying out terrain, not a real encounter format. Move these
// coordinates and the two pieces appear somewhere else on your map -- useful for
// checking that a ridge is climbable, that a bridge can be crossed, or that a piece
// can reach the far side of a valley at all.
//
// Coordinates are CUBE coordinates and MUST SUM TO ZERO: x + y + z == 0.
// That constraint is what makes them a hex grid rather than three loose numbers.
// See https://www.redblobgames.com/grids/hexagons/
//
// A coordinate that does not sum to zero is reported in the log and the unit falls
// back to the centre of the map, rather than the game refusing to start.
//
// If a coordinate has no ground the unit can stand on -- off the edge of the map, or
// a spot with too little headroom -- the unit falls back to the centre as well. Both
// cases say so in the terminal.
(
    // The piece you control. The centre of the map.
    player: (x: 0, y: 0, z: 0),

    // The enemy. Six hexes east, which is far enough to walk around before anything
    // happens and close enough to find without hunting.
    enemy: (x: 6, y: -6, z: 0),
)
